{"absolutePath":"notes/coverage/poc/P14_Ladder.sol","exportedSymbols":{"P14_Ladder":[31]},"id":32,"license":"MIT","nodeType":"SourceUnit","nodes":[{"id":1,"literals":["solidity","^","0.8",".20"],"nodeType":"PragmaDirective","src":"32:24:0"},{"abstract":false,"baseContracts":[],"canonicalName":"P14_Ladder","contractDependencies":[],"contractKind":"contract","documentation":{"id":2,"nodeType":"StructuredDocumentation","src":"58:1034:0","text":"ISOLATES: the assertion ladder \u2014 the one contribution nothing else replaces.\n `bump` moves `total` by an amount the caller chooses, but only within a\n range the guard fixes. So on the taken path there is a TRUE, PROVABLE\n statement of every strength the ladder climbs:\n   R1  post != pre\n   R2  post > pre                      (a direction)\n   R2  10 <= post - pre <= 20          (a bounded delta \u2014 the top rung)\n and `touched` gives a variable that is written unconditionally, so the\n `post == pre` rung has something to be false about.\n EXPECTED: the ladder reaches the DELTA rung here. If it stops at `!=`, the\n non-trivial-assertion rate is a property of the candidate ladder rather than\n of the contracts, and this is the smallest place that distinguishes the two.\n The delta rung also has a trap worth exercising deliberately: unsigned\n subtraction wraps, so `post - pre` must be asserted with a direction\n conjunct or the rung is true for the wrong reason."},"fullyImplemented":true,"id":31,"linearizedBaseContracts":[31],"name":"P14_Ladder","nameLocation":"1101:10:0","nodeType":"ContractDefinition","nodes":[{"constant":false,"functionSelector":"2ddbd13a","id":4,"mutability":"mutable","name":"total","nameLocation":"1133:5:0","nodeType":"VariableDeclaration","scope":31,"src":"1118:20:0","stateVariable":true,"storageLocation":"default","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint256","typeString":"uint256"},"typeName":{"id":3,"name":"uint256","nodeType":"ElementaryTypeName","src":"1118:7:0","typeDescriptions":{"type